# Spec-first workflow

This is a class assignment about structured AI-assisted development. The process matters more than the result.

## Before coding

- Do not write application code until the spec files in `/specs` exist and the user has explicitly approved them.
- Allowed before approval: planning discussions, files in `/docs`, `/specs`, and `PROCESS_LOG.md`.
- Never commit or push unless the user asks.

## Scope and implementation

- Before implementing any feature, check it against `docs/project-brief.md` and `/specs`. If it is out of scope, tell the user instead of building it.
- Work in small steps, one task at a time. After each task, stop with a short summary of what changed.
## Implementation phase
- Specs in /specs are approved and are the source of truth. Do not
  contradict them. If code and spec disagree, stop and tell me; do
  not silently change either.
- Work on one task from docs/tasks.md at a time. Stop after each
  task with a short summary and the exact commands to run the tests.
- Write the tests listed in the relevant spec together with the code
  (must-have cases first).
- All Item.status and Trade.status changes go through
  trades/services.py only.
- CRITICAL: never run git commit or git push. I do git manually.
